SUMMARY:Maya\, Give Me a Title | Adapt/Construct\, CINEkids International
  Children's Film Series
DESCRIPTION:Maya and her dad—producer and filmmaker Michel Gondry—liv
 e in two different countries. In order to stay in touch\, her dad asks he
 r every evening\, "Maya\, give me a title." Based on her answer\, he crea
 tes a short animated reply in which Maya is the hero. In this charming an
 d clever stop-motion animated adventure\, the always innovative and whims
 ical Gondry brings to life a poetic and amusing journey that will have th
 e little ones dreaming and the grown-ups smiling. [61 min\; animation\, a
 dventure\, family\; French with English subtitles]Before the screening\, 
 join us at 3pm in our lower lobby for a fun flipbook-making activity! The
 n\, on October 24\, come to the IU Sciences Library (located inside the C
 hemistry Building at 800 E. Kirkwood Ave.) anytime between 10am-4pm for a
  hands-on investigation into how things move. Show them your IU Cinema fl
 ipbook for a special sticker and goodie bag!
