SUMMARY:War Paint: Women at War | Art and a Movie
DESCRIPTION:Margy Kinmonth's feature documentary shines a light on the tr
 ailblazing role of women war artists\, on the frontlines round the world\
 , championing the female perspective on conflict through art. Culture bre
 aks the taboo\, crosses borders—tells the truth to power. Artists discu
 ssed include: Zhanna Kadyrova\, Linda Kitson\, Shirin Neshat\, Rachel Rec
 kitt\, Dame Laura Knight\, Lee Miller\, Nina Berman\, Marcelle Hanselaar\
 , Jananne Al-Ani\, Assil Diab\, Doris Zinkeisen\, Fiona Banner aka The Va
 nity Press\, Maggi Hambling\, Cornelia Parker\, Dame Rachel Whiteread\, M
 aya Lin\, and including the work of Anne Desmet R.A.\, Samar Hussaini\, a
 nd featuring Dame Penelope Lively\, Charlotte Johnstone\, and Ami Bouhass
 ane. A cast of women contributors and crew makes this film a unique under
 taking\, telling vital truths in turbulent times. War Paint: Women at War
  is the third installment in Kinmonth's trilogy of films about how artist
 s depict war\, following the acclaimed Eric Ravilious: Drawn to War and W
 ar Art with Eddie Redmayne. [89 min\; documentary\, war\; English]This pr
 ogram is presented in partnership with the Eskenazi Museum of Art. After 
 the screening\, continue the conversation at the Eskenazi Museum of Art w
 ith a special program led by museum photographer Shanti Knight. Register 
 for this free event here.
