SUMMARY:And So I Stayed w/Q&A | Additional Films and Guests
DESCRIPTION:And So I Stayed is an award-winning documentary by Natalie Pa
 ttillo and Daniel A. Nelson about survivors of abuse fighting for their l
 ives and spending years behind bars. It is a moving portrait of Kim\, Tan
 isha\, and Nikki\, three survivors whose strikingly similar stories are s
 eparated by over 30 years. None of them were believed\, and each of them 
 was criminalized for fighting back. This film is made for and by survivor
 s. For them and us to feel heard\, seen\, and believed. [91 min\; documen
 tary\; English]A panel discussion and Q&amp\;A will follow the screening 
 with co-director Natalie Pattillo\, Kerry Hyatt Bennett (Chief Legal Coun
 sel\, IN Coalition Against Domestic Violence)\, and Carrie Stillions (Exe
 cutive Director\, Middle Way House)\, moderated by Zoe Peterson (Senior S
 cientist\, Kinsey Institute\; Professor of Applied Psychology\, Education
  and Research Methodology).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><i>And So I Stayed</i> is an award-winnin
 g documentary by Natalie Pattillo and Daniel A. Nelson about survivors of
  abuse fighting for their lives and spending years behind bars. It is a m
 oving portrait of Kim\, Tanisha\, and Nikki\, three survivors whose strik
 ingly similar stories are separated by over 30 years. None of them were b
 elieved\, and each of them was criminalized for fighting back. This film 
 is made for and by survivors. For them and us to feel heard\, seen\, and 
 believed. [91 min\; documentary\; English]</p><p><i><strong>A panel discu
 ssion and Q&amp\;A will follow the screening with co-director Natalie Pat
 tillo\, Kerry Hyatt Bennett (Chief Legal Counsel\, IN Coalition Against D
 omestic Violence)\, and Carrie Stillions (Executive Director\, Middle Way
  House)\, moderated by Zoe Peterson (Senior Scientist\, Kinsey Institute\
 ; Professor of Applied Psychology\, Education and Research Methodology).<
 /strong></i></p>
